+---
+status: design-intent
+---
+
+# todo-check verifies a `path:line` citation's line number — design
+
+`scripts/todo-check.js` checks that a markdown link in a `TODO.md` entry
+resolves, and nothing else about a citation. A backticked `path:line` whose line
+is past the end of its file passes with exit 0. This closes that one gap by
+reusing the reader `scripts/memory-check.js` already has for the same shape.
+
+Approved in chat at the design gate, 2026-09-25; written here so build reads it.
+
+## 1. The check
+
+- For every entry, each backticked `path:line` span that `citations()` in `scripts/memory-check.js` returns with a line number, resolved with `resolveRef` from `scripts/docs-check.js` against the directory holding `TODO.md`, is reported as `past-end` when its line is greater than the file's line count.
+- A span whose file does not resolve is skipped, exactly as today — a missing file named only in backticks is out of scope.
+- The problem carries the entry's own line, like every other kind, so the exit code turns 1 through the existing path.
+
+## 2. Reuse
+
+- `scripts/memory-check.js` exports `lineCount`, which it already defines, so `todo-check.js` counts lines the same way `memory-check.js` does (a trailing newline is not a line).
+
+## What proves it done
+
+| test | criterion |
+|---|---|
+| `tests/todo-check.test.js` — a backticked `docs/why.md:99` against a one-line file | exits 1 and prints `past-end` and `the file ends at 1`; exits 0 before the change |
+| `tests/todo-check.test.js` — a backticked `docs/why.md:1` against the same file | exits 0 |
+| `node scripts/todo-check.js` on this repository's `TODO.md` | same exit as before the change (it holds no backticked `path:line` today) |
+
+## Files
+
+| file | change | dispatch |
+|---|---|---|
+| `scripts/memory-check.js` | add `lineCount` to `module.exports` | implementer, sonnet |
+| `scripts/todo-check.js` | a citation loop in `check()` after the link loop; `roots` from `trackedFiles(base)` | implementer, sonnet |
+| `tests/todo-check.test.js` | the two fixtures above | implementer, sonnet |
+
+Unverified: `citations()` ignores a range's end (`a.js:10-20` checks only `10`); kept as is.
