+---
+status: design-intent
+---
+
+# todo-check line-number check Implementation Plan
+
+**Goal:** `node scripts/todo-check.js` exits 1 when a `TODO.md` entry cites a backticked `path:line` past the end of its file.
+**Architecture:** `check()` in `scripts/todo-check.js` gains one loop per entry that reuses `citations()` and `lineCount()` from `scripts/memory-check.js` and `resolveRef()` from `scripts/docs-check.js`, pushing a `past-end` problem onto the existing `problems` list. No new module, no new output path.
+**Tech Stack:** Node built-ins only (`node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:test`); `npm test` is `node --test`.
+**Spec:** [2026-09-25-todo-check-line-design.md](2026-09-25-todo-check-line-design.md)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- `package.json` declares no `dependencies`; add none (CONTRIBUTING.md:36 — "new dependency" is outside a behaviour-neutral change).
+- `scripts/` is 4-space indented, `'use strict'`, CommonJS; `tests/` is 2-space indented, `node:test` + `node:assert/strict`.
+- `.fankeel/map.md`: `todo-check.js` answers "whether TODO.md is still an index" — the new problem is one more kind on the same list, not a new report section.
+- `docs.STATE_DIR` paths are runtime, never a citation — `citations()` already skips them; do not re-add them.
+- An implementer runs only `node --test tests/todo-check.test.js`; the parent runs the full `npm test` before committing.
+
+## Task 1: past-end citations in todo-check
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `scripts/todo-check.js` — require the helpers; compute `roots` once in `check()`; add the citation loop after the `linksIn` loop
+- Modify: `scripts/memory-check.js` — add `lineCount` to `module.exports`
+- Read: `scripts/docs-check.js` — `resolveRef(root, fromRel, ref)` and `PATHISH` (a path needs a `/`)
+- Read: `lib/tracked.js` — `trackedFiles(root)` returns `{ files }` with posix paths, walking when `root` is not a repository
+- Test: `tests/todo-check.test.js`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `citations(text, roots) -> [{ ref: string, wanted: number|null }]` and `lineCount(file) -> number|null` from `scripts/memory-check.js`; `resolveRef(root, fromRel, ref) -> string|null` from `scripts/docs-check.js`; `trackedFiles(root) -> { files: string[] } | null` from `lib/tracked.js`
+- Produces: `lineCount` exported from `scripts/memory-check.js`; a problem `{ line, kind: 'past-end', detail }` from `check()`
+
+**Dispatch:** implementer, sonnet — the plan carries the code; transcription plus tests.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests.** In `tests/todo-check.test.js`, after the test `'the line number points at the entry, not at the file'`, add:
+
+```js
+test('a backticked path:line past the end of its file is reported', () => {
+  const file = fixture('# TODO\n\n## Ready\n\n- Publishing — see `docs/why.md:99`.\n', { 'docs/why.md': '# why\n' });
+  const { out, code } = run(file);
+  assert.equal(code, 1);
+  assert.match(out, /past-end/);
+  assert.match(out, /docs\/why\.md:99 but the file ends at 1/);
+});
+
+test('a backticked path:line inside its file passes', () => {
+  const file = fixture('# TODO\n\n## Ready\n\n- Publishing — see `docs/why.md:1`.\n', { 'docs/why.md': '# why\n' });
+  const { code } = run(file);
+  assert.equal(code, 0);
+});
+```
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run it and watch the first fail.**
+
+```
+node --test tests/todo-check.test.js
+```
+
+Expected: `a backticked path:line past the end of its file is reported` fails on `code` (0, not 1); the second passes.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Export `lineCount`.** In `scripts/memory-check.js`, replace the `module.exports` line with:
+
+```js
+module.exports = { scan, report, parseArgs, main, projectSlug, memoryDir, indexEntries, citations, lastCommit, lineCount };
+```
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Require the helpers.** In `scripts/todo-check.js`, after `const { blameTimes } = require('../lib/blame.js');`, add:
+
+```js
+const { trackedFiles } = require('../lib/tracked.js');
+const { resolveRef } = require('./docs-check.js');
+const { citations, lineCount } = require('./memory-check.js');
+```
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Compute `roots` once.** In `scripts/todo-check.js`, in `check()`, directly after `const found = entries(text);`, add:
+
+```js
+    // The first segment of every file here, so a backticked `path:line` is
+    // read as a citation only when it is rooted somewhere this tree has —
+    // the same rule `memory-check.js` applies to the same spans.
+    const tracked = trackedFiles(base);
+    const roots = new Set((tracked ? tracked.files : []).map((f) => f.split('/')[0]));
+```
+
+- [ ] **Step 6: Add the citation loop.** In `scripts/todo-check.js`, in `check()`, inside `for (const entry of found)`, directly after the closing `}` of `for (const target of linksIn(entry.text)) { ... }`, add:
+
+```js
+        // A backticked `path:line` names a line, and a line can be deleted
+        // out from under it while the file stays. A missing file named only
+        // in backticks is not checked here; a link is how an entry says that.
+        for (const { ref, wanted } of citations(entry.text, roots)) {
+            if (wanted === null) continue;
+            const hit = resolveRef(base, '', ref);
+            if (hit === null) continue;
+            const n = lineCount(path.join(base, hit));
+            if (n !== null && wanted > n) {
+                problems.push({
+                    line: entry.line,
+                    kind: 'past-end',
+                    detail: ref + ':' + wanted + ' but the file ends at ' + n + '. Point at the line it moved to, or drop the line number.',
+                });
+            }
+        }
+```
+
+- [ ] **Step 7: Run it and watch both pass.**
+
+```
+node --test tests/todo-check.test.js
+```
+
+Expected: every test passes, including the two new ones.
+
+- [ ] **Step 8: Run it on this repository's own index.**
+
+```
+node scripts/todo-check.js
+```
+
+Expected: the same exit code and problem list as before Step 3 — `TODO.md` holds no backticked `path:line` today.
+
+- [ ] **Step 9: Commit.**
+
+```
+git add scripts/todo-check.js scripts/memory-check.js tests/todo-check.test.js
+git commit -m "fix: todo-check reports a backticked path:line past the end of its file"
+```
+
+## Coverage
+
+| promise | task |
+|---|---|
+| For every entry, each backticked `path:line` span that `citations()` in `scripts/memory-check.js` returns with a line number | Task 1 |
+| A span whose file does not resolve is skipped, exactly as today | Task 1 |
+| The problem carries the entry's own line, like every other kind | Task 1 |
+| `scripts/memory-check.js` exports `lineCount`, which it already defines | Task 1 |
+| `tests/todo-check.test.js` — a backticked `docs/why.md:99` against a one-line file | Task 1 |
+| `tests/todo-check.test.js` — a backticked `docs/why.md:1` against the same file | Task 1 |
+| `node scripts/todo-check.js` on this repository's `TODO.md` | Task 1 |
